      "message": "feat(sim): judge the probe's stylus stem and body in the protected-move law\n\nThe Probe op swept only the stylus ball against the model, so a deep\nedge or corner touch beside a taller wall, or under an overhang, passed\nwhile the stem or the probe body met the part. The law now also runs\nthe verifier's solid law (verify::solid_hits) with the probe stack from\nprobe_op::stylus_cutter: ball as the cutting atom, the stem (ball radius,\nup to the stylus length) and the probe body (plus any holder) as the\nbands. A stem or body that meets the part on any move is a ShankHit on\nthe part, a rapid that meets it RapidInStock; both hold the post. The\nexpected contact excuses nothing above the ball. The ball law is\nunchanged and a move it convicted is not reported twice.\n\nPinned by probe_reach.rs: a_stem_that_meets_an_overhang_is_a_shank_hit,\na_body_that_meets_a_tall_wall_is_a_shank_hit,\nclean_touches_stay_clean_under_the_reach_law,\nthe_stylus_stack_is_ball_then_stem_then_body,\na_short_stylus_deep_on_the_stock_edge_is_refused_by_the_op.\n\nFixes #172\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
